From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 05:42:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] tethering: do not remove clients while walking the client
 table

Turning tethering off with a client still connected logged

  g_hash_table_foreach: assertion 'version == hash_table->version' failed

unregister_all_clients() walked clients_table with g_hash_table_foreach()
and the callback, through __connman_tethering_client_unregister(),
removed the entry it was called for. GLib does not allow changing a hash
table while g_hash_table_foreach() walks it; besides the warning, it may
skip clients, which then stay listed in TetheringClients.

Use g_hash_table_foreach_remove(), which is made for this: the callback
announces the removal and returns TRUE, and GLib removes the entry.

Seen on a Q25 switching its hotspot off with a FuriPhone FLX1s connected.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/tethering.c | 16 +++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/tethering.c b/src/tethering.c
index 62258f5..2a225d4 100644
--- a/src/tethering.c
+++ b/src/tethering.c
@@ -259,16 +259,26 @@ static void tethering_restart(struct connman_ippool *pool, void *user_data)
 	g_free(ip);
 }
 
-static void unregister_client(gpointer key,
+/*
+ * Removing entries from clients_table while g_hash_table_foreach() walks
+ * it is not allowed: GLib warns ("version == hash_table->version") and
+ * may skip clients. Let g_hash_table_foreach_remove() do the removal.
+ */
+static void client_removed(const char *addr);
+
+static gboolean unregister_client(gpointer key,
 					gpointer value, gpointer user_data)
 {
 	const char *addr = key;
-	__connman_tethering_client_unregister(addr);
+
+	client_removed(addr);
+
+	return TRUE;
 }
 
 static void unregister_all_clients(void)
 {
-	g_hash_table_foreach(clients_table, unregister_client, NULL);
+	g_hash_table_foreach_remove(clients_table, unregister_client, NULL);
 }
 
 int __connman_tethering_set_enabled(const char *ip)
